# Everything here is committed for history but must not be reachable on the
# live domain. A static host serves the repo as-is, so an AdSense reviewer
# sampling URLs would otherwise find one-off patch scripts and admin panels
# and read the domain as a scratch directory rather than a published site.

# One-off patch/scrape/verify scripts from development.
scripts/

# Admin panels. Authentication is client-side only — the password is a literal
# in the page source — so these must not be publicly reachable. Run them from
# a local server against the same Firebase database instead.
admin.html
admin_records.html

# Local-only.
.env
.env.*
node_modules/
http.log
